multiCauseAndPrecedence = "An entry carries ONE deficiency and simultaneously carries every carrier this registry names. What each carrier RETAINS differs, and an earlier revision wrongly generalised the strongest case to all of them by saying the scalar `loses nothing`. The accurate statement is per carrier: resolutionCompleteness.unresolvedEdgeClasses is a genuine SET and retains EVERY applicable unresolved class at once
retainedVersusPublicRoute = "Two different routes and neither substitutes for the other. RETAINED: the whole ViewEntryV3 lives inside the coverage2 record, whose payload digest and schema digest the Run commits, so every carrier named below is retained evidence a verifier can re-derive. PUBLIC: the DEFICIENCY is projected outward as its own closed DomainDetailCode - `resolution-incomplete`, `external-consumers-unknown` and `
deficiencies:
   language-tier-unsupported -> {"carrier": "entry.nativeCause", "nativeCause": "required", "allowedCauses": ["capability-missing"], "rule": "The admitted universe's selected grammars do not bear the requested relation@rung. The cause is a single named state, so nativeCause carries it and must be exactly capability-missing. Already derived and enforced by the syntax capability prerequisite; stated here so one table covers every member."}
   provider-unavailable -> {"carrier": "entry.nativeCause", "nativeCause": "optional", "allowedCauses": ["capability-missing", "linker-unavailable"], "rule": "Section 10 leaves this row's Cause cell empty, so a null is lawful and self-describing; where a more specific named state applies it is carried. No other cause may appear."}
   input-closure-incomplete -> {"carrier": "entry.nativeCause", "nativeCause": "required", "allowedCauses": ["body-language-owner-ambiguous", "body-language-owner-unenumerated", "body-language-ownership-missing", "config-flag-stripped", "generated-file-missing", "generated-file-out-of-bounds", "generated-output-unavailable", "lockfile-missing", "missing-dependency-source", "no-program-unit", "node-modules-outside-read-set", "source-replacement-outside-snapshot"], "rule": "The one deficiency whose cause genuinely IS a single named missing input, which is why section 10 lists twelve of them and why the three body-language-* members were added here. A null refuses: this row is exactly where a null would record an unmade disclosure."}
   budget-exhausted -> {"carrier": "entry.resolutionCompleteness.stageTerminal", "nativeCause": "must-be-null", "requires": {"path": ["resolutionCompleteness", "stageTerminal"], "equals": "budget-exhausted"}, "rule": "Section 10 already qualifies this row `(stage terminal)`. The stage terminal is the cause and it is a closed StageTerminal value in the same entry, so nativeCause is null by design and the terminal must actually say budget-exhausted."}
